<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <figure class="inline-fig reveal">
    <img src="/img/Hella-B2C.webp" alt="Hella — example of consumer communication (B2C)">
    <figcaption>Consumer communication: the product as the hero of its own story.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure class="inline-fig reveal reveal-delay-1">
    <img src="/img/Hella-btob-werbeagentur-automotive.jpg" alt="Hella — example of workshop communication (B2B)">
    <figcaption>Workshop communication (B2B): the same brand, different criteria.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Hella almost never reaches the end customer directly. In between lies a growing network of independent workshops and international franchise chains that extend the value chain all the way to the vehicle owner. Each of these levels — end consumer, workshop, franchise partner — assesses the same brand by its own criteria and needs its own, yet consistent, approach.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Then there is the international dimension: what counts as premium quality in one market is already average in a technologically more advanced one. Consistent brand management has to take these gradual differences into account without reinventing the brand in every market.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 3rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Thought through channel by channel</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Instead of one communication for all, the result was a channel-specific execution: consumer communication that shows the product as the hero of its own story; online service portals and microsites for workshops; independent brand design and naming for international franchise chains; private labels for sales channels that need their own market identity.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-1">Each level — end consumer, workshop, franchise partner — assesses the same brand by its own criteria.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 3rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A channel of its own: Special OE</h2>
  <figure class="inline-fig reveal">
    <img src="/img/special-oe.jpg" alt="Hella — communication material for Special OE">
    <figcaption>Communication material for Special OE — small-series vehicle manufacturers who upgrade their vehicles with Hella premium products.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Alongside the aftermarket and franchise trade there is a third, much smaller but distinct channel: Special OE, small-series vehicle manufacturers who upgrade their vehicles with Hella premium products. This target group needs an approach tailored to specialist partners — too small for broad consumer communication, too specific for the general workshop channel.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">International, but not uniform</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Moving images for social media have to work in several languages without being produced from scratch for every market. The solution lies in language-specific lettering on a shared image base — consistent in its craft, local in its address.</p>
